    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div>Thank you for you hard work on methylKit</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m trying to import in a methylKit object a bam or a sam file.</div><div>So far I tried : </div><div>- with or without header</div><div>- deduplicated or not</div><div>- sorted or not</div><div>- sam or bam</div><div><br></div><div>none of them works so far. The main error I have is : </div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;;outline:none;border-width:initial;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;line-height:16px;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255);font-size:10.4pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"color:#606\">Trying</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> to process</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"color:#080\">/genetics/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prog</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">R_mtdna</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">exp_methyl_kit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">file</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sam<br></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">using</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> htslib</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"color:#606\">Failed</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> to read header</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> falling back</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"color:#606\">Trying</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> to process</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"color:#080\">/genetics/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prog</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">R_mtdna</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">exp_methyl_kit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">file</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sam<br></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> paired sam</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"color:#606\">Error</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> during wrapup</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"color:#008\">no</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> methylation tag found</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span></span></pre></div></code></div><br><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><div>library(methylKit)</div><div>myfile = &quot;/genetics/prog/R_mtdna/exp_methyl_kit/<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255);font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;;font-size:10.4pt;white-space:pre-wrap\">file</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">.sam&quot;</span><br></div><div>obj &lt;- processBismarkAln(myfile,&quot;test&quot;,assembly=&quot;tair10&quot;,save.folder=NULL,save.context=&quot;CpG&quot;,read.context=&quot;CpG&quot;)</div><div><br></div></div></code></div><br><br></div><div>I changed compared to the documentation the way &quot;myfile&quot; declares the file, because it is apparently not compatible anymore? (at least I have an issue with the file which is said to be non existing)</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>my data is mtdna data, with very high depth of coverage, and passed all the QC with high quality, I guess the issue is not exactly there.</div><div>I&#39;m trying to troubleshoot it but I can&#39;t find out why it doesnt work properly :/</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div></div>"
